# WSO2 Identity Server Provider

The `wso2is` provider lets you manage [WSO2 Identity Server](https://wso2.com/identity-server/) with
Terraform. You describe the setup you want in configuration files. Terraform then calls the
server's management REST APIs to create, change or delete objects until the server matches your
files.

The provider can manage these parts of the server:

* applications that sign users in with OIDC, SAML, WS-Federation or WS-Trust
* APIs and the scopes that applications may request
* users, groups, roles and user stores
* attributes (claims) and OIDC scopes
* connections to other identity providers
* organizations for business customers (B2B)
* sign-up and password recovery flows
* branding, email and SMS templates, and notification senders
* actions, webhooks and approval workflows
* tenants and tenant-wide settings

The provider is built and tested against **WSO2 Identity Server 7.3.0**. Before you start, read
[Known server behaviour and limitations](guides/server-behaviour). That page explains the server
behaviour that affects how you write configurations.

New to the provider? Follow the [Getting started](guides/getting-started) guide. It takes about
ten minutes and only needs Docker and Terraform.

